-- title:
--   The Čech complex of free abelian presheaves of a morphism is exact in positive degrees at every object
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a category with finite wide pullbacks and let $f : V \to U$ be a morphism in $\mathcal{C}$. The Čech complex of free abelian presheaves of $f$ is the chain complex $\check{C}_\bullet(f)$ with
--   $$\check{C}_n(f) = \mathbb{Z}\bigl[\,\underbrace{V \times_U \cdots \times_U V}_{n+1}\,\bigr],$$
--   the free abelian presheaf on the presheaf represented by the $(n+1)$-fold fibre product, with differentials the alternating sums of the face maps. Then for every object $W$ of $\mathcal{C}$ and every $n \ge 0$, the sequence of abelian groups obtained by evaluating at $W$,
--   $$\check{C}_{n+2}(f)(W) \xrightarrow{d} \check{C}_{n+1}(f)(W) \xrightarrow{d} \check{C}_n(f)(W),$$
--   is exact.
--
--   Together with exactness in degree $0$ (against the free presheaf on the sieve generated by $f$), this shows that the Čech complex is a resolution, which after sheafification gives the Čech resolution of the free abelian sheaf on $U$ when $f$ is a covering.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The category is `C : Type (u + 1)` with `[Category.{u} C]`, presheaves take values in `AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}`, and the complex is `cechFreePresheafComplex f : ChainComplex (Cᵒᵖ ⥤ AddCommGrpCat) ℕ`. Exactness is stated for the image of the short complex `d (n + 2) (n + 1), d (n + 1) n` under evaluation at `op W`. No covering hypothesis on `f` is needed. The Lean name is `CategoryTheory.cechFreeEval_exact_succ`.
-- source:
--   B. Bhatt, P. Scholze, The pro-étale topology for schemes, https://arxiv.org/abs/1309.1198 (v2, 17 Dec 2014). Lean source: idealson-nexources/proetale (fork of chrisflav/proetale by C. Merten, J. Jiang and contributors, Apache-2.0), commit 2983805, file Proetale/Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Sites/SheafCohomology/CechResolution.lean, lines 459-485 (`CategoryTheory.cechFreeEval_exact_succ`).

